24378:
Terminal velocity gives \eta = \frac{2r^2(\sigma - \rho)g}{9v_0}, so \eta \propto \frac{r^2}{v_0}
Log-differentiating with \sigma, \rho, g constant: \frac{\Delta\eta}{\eta} = 2\frac{\Delta r}{r} + \frac{\Delta v_0}{v_0}
Maximum error adds absolute values, matching option C → (C)

24382:
Initial kinetic energy is 2 \times \frac{1}{2}mu^2 = mu^2
Initial potential energy is \frac{kQ^2}{4R} - \frac{Gm^2}{4R} at separation 4R
Just touching at separation 2R with zero speed gives \frac{kQ^2}{2R} - \frac{Gm^2}{2R}
Energy conservation: mu^2 = \frac{kQ^2 - Gm^2}{4R}
Hence u = \sqrt{\frac{kQ^2}{4mR}(1 - \frac{Gm^2}{kQ^2})} → (C)

24384:
Each straight semi-infinite section contributes \frac{\mu_0 I}{4\pi r} along +\hat{i}
Together AB and DE act as one infinite wire giving \frac{\mu_0 I}{2\pi r}\hat{i}
The full circular loop with counter-clockwise current gives \frac{\mu_0 I}{2r}\hat{i} at O
Adding gives \frac{\mu_0 I}{2\pi r}(\pi + 1)\hat{i} → (A)

24389:
