Thus t = \frac{\pi\sqrt{LC}}{6} → (B)

24391:
Rim I = MR^2; each rod about its centre gives \frac{1}{12}M(2R)^2 = \frac{MR^2}{3}
Total I = MR^2 + \frac{2MR^2}{3} = \frac{5MR^2}{3}
Atwood with rotation: (M - m)g = (M + m)a + \frac{Ia}{R^2}
So a = \frac{(M - m)g}{M + m + 5M/3} = \frac{(M - m)g}{m + 8M/3} → (C)

24397:
