Since 2 \times 6 \times 3 \times 1.21 = 43.56 = 6.6^2, p = 6.6 \times 10^{-23}
Wavelength \lambda = \frac{h}{p} = \frac{6.6 \times 10^{-34}}{6.6 \times 10^{-23}} = 10^{-11} m
Writing 10^{-11} = \alpha \times 10^{-12} gives \alpha = 10 → (10)

